{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FIX + VERIFICATION (Gerrit change 1676).\n\nThe fix is at the two fixture sites that own the remote's storage, which covers all 16\n`push … HEAD:tickets` sites in the file at once:\n\n- `_init_bare_remote` creates the bare remote and pins `gc.autoDetach=false`,\n  `maintenance.autoDetach=false` (the posture rebar guarantees on every tracker it owns) plus\n  `receive.autogc=false`, so a push can never trigger a concurrent rewrite of the object\n  store the NEXT push depends on. A throwaway fixture remote has no reason to run upkeep.\n- `_make_repo` clones with `--no-hardlinks`, so the remote's, clone A's and clone B's object\n  stores are independent and the only thing crossing between them is what a push or fetch\n  actually transfers — which is what these tests characterize.\n\nAC3 (no masking) is satisfied by construction: the change removes a concurrent mutator. It\nadds no retry, no swallowed error, no relaxed assertion and no timing bound, and every setup\npush stays `check=True`. `test_setup_push_still_fails_when_the_push_genuinely_cannot_succeed`\npins that directly: clone B publishes a commit, clone A commits offline, and A's push is then\na true non-fast-forward that must still raise `CalledProcessError`.\n\nAC2: `test_fixture_remote_runs_no_detached_upkeep_and_shares_no_objects` asserts the posture\nand the object-store independence, converting a rare CI-only corruption into a deterministic\nlocal oracle. RED verified for BOTH limbs against a working copy with the fix removed:\n\n- pins removed -> `AssertionError: the fixture's bare remote must pin gc.autoDetach=false …\n  got ''`\n- `--no-hardlinks` removed -> `AssertionError: clone B shares 19 object file(s) with the\n  remote by hardlink`\n\nThe second is also the direct measurement that the hardlink sharing was real, not inferred.\n\nAC4: 20 consecutive runs of the file under CI's exact settings (`-n 4 --dist loadgroup`,\n`--timeout=300`), each on a fresh basetemp, with `git fsck` run over every `remote.git` the\nrun produced. Result: 20/20 with 31 passed, zero test failures and zero corrupt remotes.\n\nAC5: `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass; the full file passes (31 passed), as does the\nreconciler unit tree (2409 passed)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786566935129092001,"uuid":"c7178d47-b6b5-43e0-90c1-97a77d0dde0a"}